Changes
=======

v4.0.2 7 May 2026
  * `jws.Verify` rejects composite signatures whose trailing
    (traditional) component falls outside the variant's expected
    length: an exact match for fixed-length variants (Ed25519,
    Ed448) and a maximum DER bound for ECDSA-DER (P-256, P-384).
    Defense-in-depth: every traditional verifier in the table is
    already strict about length, but a future variant whose
    verifier ignored trailing bytes would otherwise let
    `mldsaSig || tradSig || JUNK` verify and amplify a forgery.

v4.0.1 28 Apr 2026
  * CI maintenance: bump actions/cache to 5.0.5.

v4.0.0 19 Apr 2026
  * First stable v4 release. Tracks github.com/lestrrat-go/jwx/v4 v4.0.0,
    github.com/jwx-go/ed448/v4 v4.0.0, and github.com/jwx-go/mldsa/v4 v4.0.0.

v4.0.0-alpha1 13 Apr 2026
  * Initial version. Post-quantum composite signatures for
    github.com/lestrrat-go/jwx/v4 per draft-ietf-jose-pq-composite-sigs-01.
    Covers ML-DSA-{44,65,87} paired with ES256/ES384/Ed25519/Ed448 via the
    AKP JWK key type.
